-#### Gaussian Mixture Model Visualization
-A parametric statistical model for uncertainty visualization using a mixture of Gaussians [S2]. It uses four Gaussians per mixture, chosen to consume memory comparable to quantile interpolation with eight quantiles [S2]. Memory consumption is three times the number of Gaussians in a GMM, storing mean, variance, and weight per Gaussian [S2]. It is used as a baseline parametric model for comparison against nonparametric models; RMSE is sensitive to parameter choice [S2]. Estimation of parameters such as number of Gaussians, regularization value, covariance matrix estimation, and number of MC samples can be improved to enhance quality [S2].
